(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_physics_thermodynamics=[{id:"neet-2026r-q017",pn:17,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Cyclic process heat",q:"One mole of an ideal monatomic gas undergoes a cyclic process as shown in the figure. The total heat supplied to the gas is:",o:["500 J","600 J","800 J","400 J"],c:1,s:`For any cyclic process, the change in internal energy \u0394U = 0.
Total heat exchange \u0394Q = W + \u0394U = W.
W = area of the rectangle = (300 \u2212 100)(5 \u2212 2).
W = 200 \xD7 3 = 600 J.`,fig:{w:300,h:190,alt:"P-V diagram: rectangle a b c d with a at V=2, P=300, b at V=5, P=300, c at V=5, P=100, d at V=2, P=100; the cycle runs a to b to c to d to a, clockwise.",d:[["l",53,160,53,15,"a"],["l",53,160,240,160,"a"],["t",58,12,"P [N/m\xB2]","s"],["t",244,172,"V[m\xB3]","s"],["l",49,67,57,67],["l",49,120,57,120],["t",44,71,"300","e s"],["t",44,124,"100","e s"],["l",98,156,98,164],["l",172,156,172,164],["t",98,177,"2","m s"],["t",172,177,"5","m s"],["r",98,73,75,52],["l",125,73,140,73,"a"],["l",173,92,173,106,"a"],["l",145,125,130,125,"a"],["l",98,110,98,96,"a"],["t",88,70,"a","e s"],["t",180,70,"b","s"],["t",180,138,"c","s"],["t",88,138,"d","e s"]]},sfig:{w:300,h:190,alt:"P-V diagram with dashed guide lines at P = 300 and 100 and V = 2; the rectangular cycle between V = 2 and 5 and P = 100 and 300 is drawn with clockwise arrows.",d:[["l",62,155,62,20,"a"],["l",62,155,245,155,"a"],["t",64,12,"P(N/m\xB2)","s"],["t",250,172,"V (m\xB3)","s"],["l",62,57,115,57,"d"],["l",62,118,115,118,"d"],["l",115,118,115,155,"d"],["l",199,150,199,160],["l",115,57,203,57],["l",203,57,203,118],["l",203,118,115,118],["l",115,118,115,57],["l",150,57,160,57,"a"],["l",203,80,203,92,"a"],["l",165,118,155,118,"a"],["l",115,95,115,82,"a"],["t",52,60,"300","e s"],["t",52,121,"100","e s"],["t",114,172,"2","m s"],["t",199,172,"5","m s"]]}},{id:"neet-2026-q028",pn:28,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"First law of thermodynamics",q:"An electric heater supplies heat to a system at a rate of 100 W. If the system performs work at a rate of 75 J/s, then the rate at which internal energy increases will be:",o:["125 W","100 W","25 W","75 W"],c:2,s:`First law: Q = \u0394U + W.
Differentiating with time: dQ/dt = d(\u0394U)/dt + dW/dt.
100 W = d(\u0394U)/dt + 75 W.
d(\u0394U)/dt = 25 W.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q043",pn:43,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Work in adiabatic process",q:`In an adiabatic expansion, the temperature of one mole of an ideal monatomic gas (\u03B3 = 5/3) decreases from 60 K to 50 K. The work done by the gas in the process is:
(Take the universal gas constant as R = 8.3 J mol\u207B\xB9 K\u207B\xB9)`,o:["83 J","124.5 J","166 J","41.5 J"],c:1,s:`Work done in an adiabatic process: W = nR\u0394T/(1 \u2212 \u03B3).
\u0394T = \u221210 K.
W = (1 \xD7 8.3 \xD7 (\u221210))/(1 \u2212 5/3).
W = (83 \xD7 3)/2.
W = 124.5 J.`},{id:"neet-2025-q041",pn:41,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"First law, constant pressure",q:"Two gases A and B are filled at the same pressure in separate cylinders with movable pistons of radius r_A and r_B, respectively. On supplying an equal amount of heat to both the systems reversibly under constant pressure, the pistons of gas A and B are displaced by 16 cm and 9 cm, respectively. If the change in their internal energy is the same, then the ratio r_A/r_B is equal to",o:["4/3","3/4","2/\u221A3","\u221A3/2"],c:1,s:`First law of thermodynamics: \u0394Q = \u0394U + P\u0394V.
\u0394Q is the same and \u0394U is also the same.
So W_A = W_B, i.e. (P\u0394V)_A = (P\u0394V)_B.
P is also the same, so A_A d_A = A_B d_B.
\u03C0r_A\xB2 d_A = \u03C0r_B\xB2 d_B.
r_A/r_B = (d_B/d_A)^(1/2) = (9/16)^(1/2) = 3/4.`},{id:"neet-2024-q003",pn:3,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Work done in a cyclic process (P-V graph)",q:"A thermodynamics system is taken through the cycle abcda. The work done by the gas along the path bc is-",o:["\u201390 J","\u201360 J","zero","30 J"],c:2,s:`Path bc is at constant volume (400 cm\xB3), so it is an isochoric process.
The volume does not change, so the work done by the gas along bc is zero.`,fig:{w:270,h:180,alt:"P-V graph of the cycle abcda: a at 100 cm\xB3 and 100 kPa, b at 400 cm\xB3 and 100 kPa, c at 400 cm\xB3 and 300 kPa, d at 100 cm\xB3 and 300 kPa, traversed a to b to c to d to a.",d:[["l",60,145,60,22,"a"],["l",60,145,250,145,"a"],["t",52,20,"P","e"],["t",215,172,"V"],["l",225,168,248,168,"a"],["l",60,50,110,50,"d"],["l",60,90,110,90,"d"],["l",110,90,110,145,"d"],["l",190,90,190,145,"d"],["t",55,54,"300 kPa","e"],["t",55,94,"100 kPa","e"],["t",110,162,"100 cm\xB3","m"],["t",190,162,"400 cm\xB3","m"],["l",110,90,155,90,"a"],["l",155,90,190,90],["l",190,90,190,68,"a"],["l",190,68,190,50],["l",190,50,150,50,"a"],["l",150,50,110,50],["l",110,50,110,72,"a"],["l",110,72,110,90],["t",102,46,"d","e"],["t",196,46,"c"],["t",196,96,"b"],["t",116,102,"a"]]}},{id:"neet-2023-q018",pn:18,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Carnot engine efficiency",q:"A Carnot engine has an efficiency of 50% when its source is at a temperature 327\xB0 C. The temperature of the sink is:",o:["200\xB0C","27\xB0C","15\xB0C","100\xB0C"],c:1,s:`Efficiency = 50/100 = 1/2.
Source temperature T\u2081 = 327 + 273 = 600 K.
Efficiency = 1 \u2212 T\u2082/T\u2081, so 1/2 = 1 \u2212 T\u2082/600.
T\u2082/600 = 1/2, so T\u2082 = 300 K.
T\u2082 = 300 \u2212 273 = 27\xB0C.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q016",pn:16,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Polytropic process PV\xB2 = C",q:"An ideal gas follows a process described by the equation PV\xB2 = C from the Initial (P\u2081, V\u2081, T\u2081) to final (P\u2082, V\u2082, T\u2082) thermodynamic states, where C is a constant. Then:",o:["If P\u2081 > P\u2082 then V\u2081 > V\u2082","If P\u2081 > P\u2082 then V\u2081 < V\u2082","If V\u2082 > V\u2081 then T\u2082 > T\u2081","If V\u2082 > V\u2081 then T\u2082 < T\u2081"],c:3,s:`PV\xB2 = C and PV = nRT together give TV = constant, and also T\xB2/P = constant.
So if P increases, V decreases; if T increases, V decreases; and T and P rise or fall together.
If V\u2082 > V\u2081 then T\u2082 < T\u2081 (since TV is constant).
Also P\u2081 > P\u2082 means V\u2082 > V\u2081 and T\u2081 > T\u2082, which shows options (1) and (2) are the wrong way round.`},{id:"neet-2022-q020",pn:20,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"P-V curves of processes",q:"An ideal gas undergoes four different processes from the same initial state as shown in the figure below. Those processes are adiabatic, isothermal, isobaric and isochoric. The curve which represents the adiabatic process among 1, 2, 3 and 4 is",o:["2","3","4","1"],c:0,s:`Slope of the adiabatic curve: dP/dV = \u2013\u03B3P.
Slope of the isothermal curve: dP/dV = \u2013P.
Since \u03B3 > 1, the adiabatic curve is steeper.
Of the two falling curves, the steeper one (2) is adiabatic.`,fig:{w:240,h:200,alt:"P-V graph with four curves from one point: 4 horizontal, 3 and 2 falling curves with 2 steeper, 1 vertical.",d:[["l",20,175,20,11.800000000000011,"a"],["l",20,175,224,175,"a"],["t",14.9,8.400000000000006,"P","e"],["t",218.9,197.1,"V","m"],["l",51.45,33.05000000000001,190,33.05000000000001],["p","M51.5 33.1C56.4 37.3 70.6 51 81.2 58.6C91.8 66.1 103.9 73.1 115.2 78.1C126.5 83.1 139 85.9 149.2 88.3C159.4 90.7 171.9 91.8 176.4 92.6"],["p","M51.5 33.1C55 39.4 64.2 59.5 72.7 71.3C81.2 83.1 91.1 95.8 102.5 103.6C113.8 111.4 128.4 114.9 140.7 118.1C153 121.2 170.5 121.6 176.4 122.3"],["l",51.45,33.05000000000001,51.45,146.1],["t",198.5,37.30000000000001,"4"],["t",183.2,96.8,"3"],["t",183.2,125.7,"2"],["t",55.699999999999996,158,"1"]]},sfig:{w:280,h:200,alt:"P-V graph labelled: horizontal line isobaric, upper falling curve isothermal, lower steeper curve adiabatic, vertical line isochoric.",d:[["l",20,175,20,11.800000000000011,"a"],["l",20,175,224,175,"a"],["t",14.9,8.400000000000006,"P","e"],["t",218.9,197.1,"V","m"],["l",51.45,33.05000000000001,190,33.05000000000001],["p","M51.5 33.1C56.4 37.3 70.6 51 81.2 58.6C91.8 66.1 103.9 73.1 115.2 78.1C126.5 83.1 139 85.9 149.2 88.3C159.4 90.7 171.9 91.8 176.4 92.6"],["p","M51.5 33.1C55 39.4 64.2 59.5 72.7 71.3C81.2 83.1 91.1 95.8 102.5 103.6C113.8 111.4 128.4 114.9 140.7 118.1C153 121.2 170.5 121.6 176.4 122.3"],["l",51.45,33.05000000000001,51.45,146.1],["t",198.5,37.30000000000001,"Isobaric"],["t",183.2,96.8,"Isothermal"],["t",183.2,125.7,"Adiabatic"],["t",51.45,164.8,"Isochoric","m"]]}},{id:"neet-2020-q101",pn:101,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Free expansion",q:"Two cylinders A and B of equal capacity are connected to each other via a stop cock. A contains an ideal gas at standard temperature and pressure. B is completely evacuated. The entire system is thermally insulated. The stop cock is suddenly opened. The process is :",o:["adiabatic","isochoric","isobaric","isothermal"],c:3,s:`The gas expands into vacuum, so it does no work (W = 0).
The system is insulated, so no heat flows (Q = 0).
So \u0394U = 0 and, for an ideal gas, \u0394T = 0.
The temperature stays the same, so the printed key (isothermal) is taken.
Note: Printed key 4 (isothermal) kept; Q = 0 also makes the process adiabatic, but the temperature does not change.`},{id:"neet-2019-q106",pn:106,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Thermodynamic processes",q:"In which of the following processes, heat is neither absorbed nor released by a system ?",o:["isobaric","isochoric","isothermal","adiabatic"],c:3,s:"In an adiabatic process there is no exchange of heat, so Q = 0."},{id:"neet-2018-q009",pn:9,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"First law of thermodynamics",q:"A sample of 0.1 g of water at 100\xBAC and normal pressure (1.013 \xD7 10\u2075 Nm\u207B\xB2) requires 54 cal of heat energy to convert to steam at 100\xBAC. If the volume of the steam produced is 167.1 cc, the change in internal energy of the sample, is",o:["104.3 J","208.7 J","42.2 J","84.5 J"],c:1,s:`Heat given Q = 54 \xD7 4.18 = 225.72 J.
Initial volume of 0.1 g water = 0.1 cc.
Work done by the system W = P\u0394V = 1.013 \xD7 10\u2075 \xD7 (167.1 \u2013 0.1) \xD7 10\u207B\u2076 = 16.91 J.
First law: \u0394U = Q \u2013 W = 225.72 \u2013 16.91 = 208.7 J.`},{id:"neet-2018-q034",pn:34,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Work and heat in isobaric process",q:"The volume (V) of a monatomic gas varies with its temperature (T), as shown in the graph. The ratio of work done by the gas, to the heat absorbed by it, when it undergoes a change form state A to stage B, is",o:["(2)/(5)","(2)/(3)","(1)/(3)","(2)/(7)"],c:0,s:`The graph of V against T is a straight line through the origin, so V \u221D T and the pressure is constant (isobaric).
W = nR\u0394T and Q = nCp\u0394T, so (W)/(Q) = (R)/(Cp).
For a monatomic gas Cp = (5)/(2)R.
(W)/(Q) = (R)/((5/2)R) = (2)/(5).`,fig:{w:260,h:185,alt:"Graph of V against T: a straight line from the origin O rising to the right, with points A and B on it and an arrow from A to B.",d:[["l",60,150,60,20,"a"],["l",60,150,230,150,"a"],["t",54,24,"V","e"],["t",236,154,"T",""],["t",50,164,"O","e"],["l",60,150,210,70,""],["l",124,115.5,162,95,"a"],["c",120,118,2.6,"F"],["c",165,94,2.6,"F"],["t",108,108,"A","e"],["t",168,84,"B",""]]}},{id:"neet-2018-q036",pn:36,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Thermodynamics",st:"Efficiency of Carnot engine",q:"The efficiency of an ideal heat engine working between the freezing point and boiling point of water, is",o:["26.8%","20%","6.25%","12.5%"],c:0,s:`Sink T\u2082 = 0\xB0C = 273 K and source T\u2081 = 100\xB0C = 373 K.
\u03B7 = 1 \u2013 (T\u2082)/(T\u2081) = 1 \u2013 (273)/(373) = 1 \u2013 0.732 = 0.268.
Efficiency = 26.8%.`}]})();
